          "new_text": "def matrix_free_spectral_embedding(\n    counts: np.ndarray,\n    n_components: int,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Return leading spectral coordinates for a cell-by-feature count matrix.\"\"\"\n    # input validation\n    if not isinstance(counts, np.ndarray) or counts.ndim != 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"counts must be a 2D numpy array\")\n    if not np.all(np.isfinite(counts)):\n        raise ValueError(\"counts must be finite\")\n    if np.any(counts < 0):\n        raise ValueError(\"counts must be nonnegative\")\n    if np.any(counts.sum(axis=1) == 0):\n        raise ValueError(\"all-zero cell rows not allowed\")\n    n_cells = counts.shape[0]\n    if not (1 <= n_components < n_cells):\n        raise ValueError(\"n_components must be 1 <= n_components < n_cells\")\n    # matrix-free operator for Gram matrix: counts @ counts.T\n    from scipy.sparse.linalg import LinearOperator, eigsh\n    def matvec(x):\n        return counts @ (counts.T @ x)\n    A = LinearOperator((n_cells, n_cells), matvec=matvec, dtype=counts.dtype)\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(random_state)\n    v0 = rng.randn(n_cells)\n    eigenvalues, eigenvectors = eigsh(A, k=n_components, which='LM', v0=v0)\n    # sort descending\n    idx = np.argsort(eigenvalues)[::-1]\n    eigenvalues = eigenvalues[idx]\n    eigenvectors = eigenvectors[:, idx]\n    return eigenvalues, eigenvectors"
